The fork was imported with its full git history at upstream commit
f0e2116001af5a1bbf39481535f837d6a25772e8. The tag step/00-import is the
import merge commit 2badf67, whose second parent is f0e2116; that merge
itself replaced README.md with the fork's README and added README-lcpc.md, a
byte-identical copy of upstream's README.md (`git diff f0e2116 step/00-import`
shows exactly these two files). Every later change is a commit in this
repository; `git log step/00-import..HEAD` lists them, and the tags
step/01-modernize ... step/09-codegen mark one technique per tag.

Changes made by the RealBrakedownPerf authors (2026), Apache-2.0:

- Modified upstream files. Each carries a "Modified 2026 by the
  RealBrakedownPerf authors" comment after its upstream header:
    Cargo.toml (workspace), .gitignore,
    lcpc-2d/Cargo.toml, lcpc-2d/src/{lib,tests}.rs,
    lcpc-brakedown-pc/Cargo.toml,
    lcpc-brakedown-pc/src/{codespec,encode,lib,matgen,tests}.rs,
    lcpc-ligero-pc/Cargo.toml, lcpc-ligero-pc/src/{lib,tests}.rs,
    lcpc-test-fields/Cargo.toml, lcpc-test-fields/src/lib.rs.
  README.md was replaced by the fork's README (in the import merge
  step/00-import, and edited since); the upstream README is kept unchanged
  as README-lcpc.md.
  Summary: current dependencies and stable Rust; column-major batched
  encoding; R2L evaluation with transposed graphs and runtime code
  parameters; lazy reduction through the LazyField trait; multi-edge
  blocking; LLC slicing; an expander-level worker pool; portable codegen
  tuning.
- Removed upstream files: upstream's nightly #[bench] harnesses
  lcpc-brakedown-pc/src/bench.rs and lcpc-ligero-pc/src/bench.rs (replaced
  by the stable benchmark crate bench/).
- New files in upstream crates: lcpc-brakedown-pc/src/{cache,graph,
  thread_pool}.rs and lcpc-test-fields/src/fft.rs (see below).
- New crates and files: lcpc-fields/, lcpc-oracle-tests/,
  lcpc-spielman-oracle/, bench/, reproduce/, external/, docs/, tests/golden/,
  tools/, results/, NOTICE, rust-toolchain.toml, .cargo/config.toml,
  Cargo.lock, and every file under scripts/ except upstream's
  scripts/microbench.sh and scripts/print_bench.sh (unchanged).

Code derived from fffft:

- lcpc-test-fields/src/fft.rs is a modified copy of src/lib.rs of fffft
  0.4.2 (https://crates.io/crates/fffft, upstream LCPC's FFT dependency of
  lcpc-ligero-pc), Copyright 2020 Riad S. Wahby <rsw@cs.stanford.edu>,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the same license text as
  LICENSE). It was embedded because fffft 0.4.2 requires ff 0.12; the
  changes port it to ff 0.14, remove its nightly benchmark code, and keep
  adapted versions of two of fffft's tests (roundtrip, roots_of_unity) as
  an inline test module. The file keeps its original copyright
  notice and states the change.

Third-party baselines used only for comparison are not part of this product's
source and keep their own licenses:

- SIMD-Spielman-for-ZKPs (upstream commit 7b399db), Copyright 2026 Florian
